<!--
  https://sudoroom.org/events/feed/ as surveyed 2026-08-05, trimmed from 1715
  items to six.

  THE ONE GENUINE CASE IN THE REGISTRY. <pubDate> here is the EVENT START, not
  the publish time: WP Events Manager runs the `event` post type through the
  ordinary feed and dates each item with the event. That is a per-source fact,
  it is declared in sources.yaml as `pubdate_means: event_start`, and nothing in
  the adapter infers it — the same six items with `post_date` declared emit no
  events at all.

  The six cover, in order:
    1. an ordinary -0700 (PDT) start
    2. a second one on the same evening, to keep the sort order honest
    3. a UTC 'GMT' start, which RFC 5322 permits and this feed does emit
    4. a '-0000' start: RFC 5322's "local time unknown". Naive on purpose.
    5. an item with NO pubDate at all — dropped and counted, never assumed
    6. a start well past a 120-day horizon opened on 2026-08-05
-->
